From 3e1eb762232b5e9d51ce33e18cb4d87762fceff3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 08:00:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arch/dadao: implement maskable async dispatch core (KL-131a)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds SEE §5 steps 2-6 (nonmaskable bypass, inner_cfx_mask/global_cfx_mask/
excp_cause_mask arbitration, trap/sync/async counters) as a shared gate
(ISA::cfxDispatch()) in front of KL-122a's precise-entry carrier
(ISA::cfxPreciseTrapEnter(), steps 7-10), mirroring QEMU's
dadao_cfx_dispatch() field-for-field. All three prior call sites
(cfx_smon CFXTRAP, cfx_ptw CFXTRAP-as-call, cfx_ptw/cfx_tlb fault delivery
via tlb.cc) are nonmaskable and route through unchanged behaviorally
except for the new trap/sync counters.

New architectural state: cg0-3/rc1 shared global_cfx_mask
(cfxModeGlobalCfxMask[4], one per mode, not per cfxcode -- the wiki
explicitly marks this register shared), cg0-3/rc11 per-cfx/mode
excp_cause_mask, cg5/rc63 RO excp_cause_nonmaskable (hardware-static per
cfx cause table, cfxExcpCauseNonmaskableFor()), cg4/rc2-4 HW trap_num/
excp_sync_num/excp_async_num counters. cfxCommonPendingMask() (the per-cfx
maskable-cause table) moved from decoder.cc-local static to a shared
isa.hh/isa.cc function so isa.cc's dispatch/scan logic can reuse it.

New instruction-boundary asynchronous dispatch: Interrupts::
checkInterrupts()/getInterrupt() (previously stub, always false/NoFault)
now perform a real scan (ISA::cfxAsyncScan()) implementing contracts/isa/
spec.md §8.5.1's frozen priority rule (lowest pending eligible cfxcode,
then lowest eligible cause bit), delivered via a new AsyncInterruptFault
whose invoke() calls ISA::cfxDispatch(isSync=false). Unlike QEMU (which
batches multiple guest instructions per translation block and needs an
explicit max_insns=1 forcing hack for instruction-boundary precision),
gem5's AtomicSimpleCPU already checks interrupts once per tick() = once
per instruction, so no equivalent gate is needed -- but this only fires in
FullSystem mode (BaseCPU::checkInterrupts()'s own `FullSystem &&` gate),
so the new async probes run via tests/dadao/dadao_fs.py (KL-124a's
FullSystem bare-metal carrier), not the SE-mode harness prior K1 probes
used. dadao_fs.py gained --cfx-async-level-a/-b CLI options wiring the two
new test-only level-source params through to system.cpu.isa[0].

Test-only additions (never guest-visible ABI, mirroring QEMU): a
synchronous dispatch trigger (cg4/rc60, CfxTestSyncDispatchCg/Rc) letting
a test program directly invoke the steps 2-6 gate with an arbitrary
(target, cause, isSync=true) triple -- needed because M1's only real
maskable synchronous cause (FPEXCP) has no execution path (RF excluded
from M1); two independent persistent level-triggered async test sources
(cfxAsyncTestLevelA/BCode/Seed SimObject params) driving the new
instruction-boundary delivery probes.

ISA::cfxDispatch() takes both isSync and stageSequentialAdvance as
independent bool parameters (unlike QEMU, which only needs is_sync): the
former selects counter/redirect semantics, the latter is passed straight
through to cfxPreciseTrapEnter()'s existing PC pre-compensation staging
and must be true when called from within a normal instruction's own
execute() (its own subsequent advancePC() needs pre-compensation) and
false when the entry replaces fetch entirely (PTW/TLB fault ReExec, and
the async fault's invoke(), both outside any instruction's execute()).

Zero regression: KL-113a/117a/120a/122a/124a/125a/126a/127a/129a probes,
81/81 lit E2E, run_differential.py (AGREE(3-way)=200, AGREE(4-way)=200,
zero DIVERGE), manifest_check.py, check_issues.py all unchanged from
baseline (verified from the DADAO-0628 root repo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
